# DebugSwift Tools — environment
#
# THE APP RUNS WITHOUT ANY OF THESE. A fresh clone builds, all eight tools work,
# and the website audit runs its 34 checks end to end with nothing configured.
# Every tool here is arithmetic, parsing, or one outbound HTTP request.
#
# ONE OPTIONAL KEY, added 23 Aug 2026. Until then this file was deliberately
# empty and said so. It is worth being precise about what changed: the audit's
# own checks still need nothing. The key buys one extra, opt-in section — the
# "deeper checks" button, which asks Google, Mozilla and a domain registry about
# the page. Without the key that section renders and says PageSpeed is not
# configured on this deployment; the other two still answer. Nothing else in the
# app degrades.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PAGESPEED_API_KEY   (optional, server-only, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — ever)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google PageSpeed Insights v5. Free, no card, 25,000 queries a day.
#   console.cloud.google.com → enable "PageSpeed Insights API" → create an API
#   key → restrict it to that one API.
#
# It has to be a key rather than nothing: unauthenticated PSI requests from a
# shared server address are answered 429 on the first try. Verified 23 Aug 2026.
#
# PAGESPEED_API_KEY=
#
# THE VARIABLE THAT LIVES ELSEWHERE: TOOLS_ORIGIN is set on the MARKETING
# project (E:\debugswift), not here. It points the reverse proxy at this
# deployment's URL, e.g. https://debugswift-tools.vercel.app. Setting it here
# does nothing.
#
# If you add a key:
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined at BUILD time and ship in the browser
#     bundle. Setting one without redeploying changes nothing, and it is not a
#     secret. The marketing repo lost time to exactly this.
#   - Anything genuinely secret must be server-only and must never be read from
#     a component.
